# Android Studio preview (سبزینه)

This workspace is the source of truth:

`C:\Users\Mohamadi\Desktop\sabzine\sabzine`

Android Studio is opened on a second copy:

`%USERPROFILE%\source\repos\سبزینه`

The Flutter project is the `app/` directory (`app/pubspec.yaml`). Android Studio must open that app root, not the monorepo root.

After you **create, edit, or delete** any project file (especially under `app/lib/`, `app/test/`, `app/assets/`, `app/android/`, `app/pubspec.yaml`), run:

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tool/sync_android_studio.ps1
```

Do this before ending the task so the user can preview in Android Studio without manual copy.

Do not edit only the `source\repos\سبزینه` path; always change files in this workspace, then sync.

Optional long-term fix: close Android Studio, rename the old `source\repos\سبزینه` folder, and create a directory junction to the `app` folder so sync is unnecessary.
